      "problem": "If $|5x-12|=3,$ then $x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|5x-12|=5x-12,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5x-12| & =3 \\\\ 5x-12 & =3 \\\\ 5x & =15 \\\\ \\frac{5x}{5} & =\\frac{15}{5} \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|5x-12|=-(5x-12),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5x-12| & =3 \\\\ -(5x-12) & =3 \\\\ -5x+12 & =3 \\\\ -5x & =-9 \\\\ \\frac{-5x}{-5} & =\\frac{-9}{-5} \\\\ x & =\\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\frac{9}{5}$ and $x=3.$",
